# Tracked: everything needed to build and flash our custom firmware.
# Ignored: everything else.

# --- machine-specific settings ---
config/local.toml
.claude/launch.json
/.claude/handoff

# --- build artifacts (regenerated by tools/build.py) ---
build/

# --- Buchla's Windows kit ---
# The flashing tools inside it are third-party and GPL-licensed, so they ship
# here alongside the macOS ones (see THIRD-PARTY.md).  What does not ship is
# Buchla's own material: the firmware image, their updater and their notes.
#
# Buchla's windows/ folder is vendor drop except the three tools the flasher
# runs, which were force-added; the launcher/ sources and its built exe are
# ours and tracked.  A directory a pattern excludes cannot have files
# re-included, so the folders come back first, then their junk goes again.
windows/*
!windows/support/
windows/support/*
!windows/support/dfu-programmer.exe
!windows/support/sendmidi.exe
!windows/support/zadig-2.8.exe
!windows/launcher/
windows/launcher/*
!windows/launcher/launcher.c
!windows/launcher/launcher.rc
!windows/launcher/AppIcon.svg
!windows/launcher/AppIcon.ico
!windows/launcher/218e Rewired Flasher.exe

# Stock firmware images for other models/versions.
otherfirmware/

# Buchla's original updater and its docs — kept out so the experimental
# updater is never confused with the factory one.
ProgramLEM218.command
Buchla 218 Firmware Flashing Guide.pdf
changelog.txt
# The rule above is for stray copies out of downloaded packages; the
# repository CHANGELOG.txt is a source file (the page embeds it and the
# packages ship it), and on a case-insensitive filesystem the rule
# would swallow it silently.
!/CHANGELOG.txt

# Diagnostic updater, rebuilt on demand alongside the latch-probe image.
ProgramLEM218_LatchProbe.command

# --- firmware images ---
# No firmware image is distributed from this repository.
#
# The factory image is Buchla's, and is not ours to redistribute; you already
# have it if you have the official flashing kit.  The patched image is that
# same firmware with our patches spliced in, so it is not ours to redistribute
# either.  What this repository ships is the recipe: put your own factory
# image at the path in config/218e.toml and build.
firmware/*.hex

# Never let a firmware image sit in the served web directory.
web/*.hex

# Written by the flasher: what is actually on the instrument.
firmware/INSTALLED.txt

# --- captures, logs, scratch ---
# Pressure measurements from one particular instrument.
LEM218_PressureReadout.csv
LEM218_PressureReadout_*.csv
PressureReadout_Protocol.md

# Flash logs: per-run, per-machine, and they name local paths.
*_flash_log.txt
*_fwflash_log.txt
218e_v3_Rewired_flash_log.txt

*_analysis/
ghidra_project/
*.gpr
*.rep/

# --- hardware working files ---
# Photoshop scan of the pressure op-amp section (~81 MB).
PRESSURE_OPAMP.psd

.DS_Store

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The complete licensed Euclid package, copied in for reference.  This repo is
# public: committing it would publish a commercial font wholesale, including
# the desktop .otf/.ttf.  Only the four WebXL woff2 the page actually loads
# live in web/fonts/, and even those are a licensing decision - see
# THIRD-PARTY.md.
web/font/
web/kit/

# The long firmware write-up is the working reference behind the patches - it
# names addresses, dead ends and an unreleased project, and it is written for
# whoever is next in Ghidra, not for an owner.  Kept locally, published as the
# short docs/FIRMWARE_CHANGES.md instead.
docs/internals/

# Not everything that runs against this project belongs in it.
private/
/deploy/.wrangler/cache

# The FCP video kit lives in its own private repo (fcp/ is a nested checkout).
fcp/
